      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page, [[write-journal]], describes a transactional mechanism that the guarded tool executor uses to ensure all-or-nothing semantics for file writes. \n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n- Before any file is overwritten, the system first records the file\u0027s prior state into an in-memory journal \u2014 capturing either its previous content or noting that it didn\u0027t exist.\n- If the agent run fails (due to exceeding turn limits, unrecoverable errors, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order, restoring previous file content or deleting newly created files.\n- This provides transaction-like guarantees without needing a database \u2014 the in-memory journal itself acts as the transaction log, lasting only for the duration of a single run.\n- The Query agent doesn\u0027t use the rollback capability since it has no write tool, though the journal type exists in the shared runtime library.",
      "input_tokens": 5374,
      "output_tokens": 207
    }
